From 90570a2fb5d1b256c8a6feae75f882bfe9380247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:57:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/exynos: decon7: expose the third hardware window

The Exynos7870 DECON has three composition windows, but the driver only
ever registered two of them, one of which is the cursor plane.  Every
additional layer therefore has to be composited by the GPU, even when
the hardware could stack it for free.

Evidence that three windows are available on this SoC:

  - the vendor device tree declares max_win = <3>;
  - the vendor CAL layer only maps IDMA_G0 and IDMA_G1 to a non-zero
    WINCHMAP channel, window 0 having its own path;
  - reading the block on a live system shows WINCON0..2 at their reset
    value 0x0001e000 while WINCON3..5 read 0, and SHADOWCON has the
    protect bits of windows 0, 1 and 2 set.

The per-window register accessors (WINCON, VIDOSD_A..D, VIDW_*, BLENDE)
are already indexed correctly, and all five loops over WINDOWS_NR are
generic, so exposing the extra window needs no other change.  The DMA
channel mapping in WINCHMAP0 is left untouched: the bootloader programs
window 1 to IDMA_G0 and window 2 to IDMA_G1, and the value survives the
driver's reset sequence.

zpos stays immutable because the DECON blends its windows in a fixed
order; decon_bind() already assigns zpos = window index.

Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
index fb199eed7f..be547a0e7c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 
 #define MIN_FB_WIDTH_FOR_16WORD_BURST 128
 
-#define WINDOWS_NR	2
+#define WINDOWS_NR	3
 
 struct decon_data {
 	unsigned int vidw_buf_start_base;
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@ static const uint32_t decon_formats[] = {
 
 static const enum drm_plane_type decon_win_types[WINDOWS_NR] = {
 	DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY,
+	DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY,
 	DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR,
 };
 
